{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
  "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nJEFFREY L. FISHER, ESQ., Stanford, California; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nMATTHEW R. McGUIRE, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General of Virginia, Richmond, Virginia; on behalf of the Respondent.\nERICA L. ROSS, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, in support of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Doesn't it -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Kagan, it would not be okay under Virginia law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is because, if -- if the prosecution gets a conviction, the prosecution can choose to try its stronger claim first."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, we don't have a problem leaving severance decisions to trial judges according to the various rules across the country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Fisher, don't we have a case that says this issue preclusion is only between the same parties?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When an acquittal happens, the prosecution then may well drop the second charges."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is -- is there anything to indicate that the result would be different -- would have been different in Jeffers if the first trial had been an acquittal?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the Double Jeopardy Clause does already distinguish in multiple ways between acquittals and convictions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McGuire",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, when a defendant agrees to have multiple trials, he gives up his right to argue that the later trial is barred based on double jeopardy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0001-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, by the way, if the prosecutor has a problem, he can always insist on a written waiver if the defendant really wants the separate trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McGuire",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McGUIRE: -- of inconsistent verdicts. JUSTICE KAGAN: -- Mr. McGuire, I mean, it's one thing to say, as we've said many times, that when you say I want two trials, that what you've given up is the right to object about two trials. Right? That really is inconsistent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Can we -- can we clear up one thing about this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Which, the second?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But we don't permit you to try a person for robbing one person and then try the second crime, which is not technically distinct, it's distinct completely, there are different people involved."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He's waiving a constitutional right and, therefore, why shouldn't it be express? And that's -- that is where I think I stop because I want to know your answer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What would have happened here if the defendant got up and said Virginia law requires separate trials. I won't -- I want what the law gives me. I won't waive my double jeopardy rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0003-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Four minutes, Mr. Fisher."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think I heard two separate ways to look at this case, and I want to respond to each of them. So my friend from Virginia, in particular with just -- in a colloquy with Justice Kagan, says the only way issue preclusion works is that you invoke it at the outset of the second trial and, if you cannot bar the second trial at that point, it drops away and the right is gone."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f5455fec8c53da4f1c140f162bbbd602fd79a3f286f1ac0d93f93225763fe61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f5455fec8c5-0003-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it can even allow the second trial to go forward, just simply in a manner that doesn't allow the prosecution functionally to try the defendant for the same offense twice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1348",
      "confidence": 0.0,
